# Local WoT graph and relay sync

## Do not edit `src/graph/trust`

[`src/graph/trust`](../../src/graph/trust) is the vendored Trust heap graph
(DigitalTrustProtocol/Trust). Do **not** modify it without explicit
permission. The package is fragile under AI interference. Change AttentionX
wrappers instead: `src/graph/graph.ts`, `adapter.ts`, `query.ts`,
`identity-index-resolver.ts`, `ratings/`.

## Product rules

- Trust results are subjective evidence for the local root, context, and bounds — never an objective or universal score.
- Preserve direct evidence, paths, source event IDs, graph version, and truncation state in query results.
- Kind `32009` only for trust statements; kind `32014` for ratings (never hops). Optional `l` labels augment either with human clarification and are not hops.
- Scope (`s`) is **not** part of graph slot identity or resolve. Handle it at publish, relay filter, and ingest eligibility. See [docs/architecture.md § Scope policy](../../docs/architecture.md#scope-policy-attentionx-on-xcom).

## Hot path vs durable state

- Timeline CPU first: scroll queries must stay in-memory lookups. A slow graph rebuild or per-cell RPC makes the feed unresponsive; if that happens, nothing else matters. See `docs/architecture.md` § Timeline CPU and responsiveness.
- Durable source of truth: current winning signed events (+ indexes) in IndexedDB — not a full history of replaced addressable slots.
- Hot path: in-memory graph in the service worker answering `QUERY_TRUST` / `QUERY_TRUST_BATCH` and `QUERY_RATING` / `QUERY_RATING_BATCH` without IndexedDB per lookup.
- Prefer a personal graph snapshot in IndexedDB for fast rehydrate after SW restart (see `docs/architecture.md` § Hot trust graph) — do not rely on immortal SW memory alone.
- Validate and reduce on ingest; avoid rebuilding the graph by re-validating every stored event on SW wake.
- Do not invent content-script `GRAPH_KEEPALIVE` or offscreen-document graph holders unless implementing that design deliberately.

## Bounds

- Sync and traversal are depth/fan-out/author/event bounded; follow only active positive `p` edges for expansion.
- `p` subjects are traversable; X account/post `i` subjects are terminal evidence.
- Advance relay cursors after EOSE with an overlap window; dedupe by event ID across relays.
- Kind `32009` relay pulls on x.com must cover **`#s=x.com` and empty-scope** events (user trusts omit `s`; post trusts use `x.com`). See `src/relay/filters.ts` and architecture scope policy.
- Product Graph snapshot, neighborhood, and Path trust queries walk `c=identity`. Post rating overlays query empty context. Traversal still follows only Trust (`1`) `p` hops; Neutral (`0`) edges may be visualized.

## What not to use

- `chrome.storage.local` / `session` for the large personal WoT.
- Per-tab content-script graph caches as the source of truth.
